{"item_id": "B00A1TCULW", "title": "Ruger LCP Magazine Pocket Protector", "description": "So you carry a concelaed pistol? If you didn't you probably wouldn't be here on this website looking at our product. So what happens if you ever need to use that pistol? In most cases you'd be limited to 6, 7, or maybe even 8 shots unless you carry a spare magazine. But carrying an extra magazine can be as much hassle as carrying a firearm. Where do you put it? Your pocket? Be careful, keys, change, or even a pocket knife can make pocket carrying a loaded magazine a dangerous idea. That's where the Sneaky Pete Ruger LCP Magazine Pocket Protector comes in. These leather pocket protectors protect your magazines and prevent anything in your pocket from touching them. They're an inexpensive and convenient way to double or even triple your firepower. Carry more ammunition and look good while doing it. Our Magazine Pocket Protectors are made from the exact same leather as our holsters. Soft, strong, and good looking. Can you think of a good reason NOT to buy one? We can't.", "text": "Ruger LCP Magazine Pocket Protector So you carry a concelaed pistol? If you didn't you probably wouldn't be here on this website looking at our product. So what happens if you ever need to use that pistol? In most cases you'd be limited to 6, 7, or maybe even 8 shots unless you carry a spare magazine. But carrying an extra magazine can be as much hassle as carrying a firearm. Where do you put it? Your pocket? Be careful, keys, change, or even a pocket knife can make pocket carrying a loaded magazine a dangerous idea. That's where the Sneaky Pete Ruger LCP Magazine Pocket Protector comes in. These leather pocket protectors protect your magazines and prevent anything in your pocket from touching them. They're an inexpensive and convenient way to double or even triple your firepower. Carry more ammunition and look good while doing it. Our Magazine Pocket Protectors are made from the exact same leather as our holsters. Soft, strong, and good looking. Can you think of a good reason NOT to buy one? We can't.", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/610o0IxL8NL._SY300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B00A1TCULW.jpg", "metadata": {"categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Hunting & Fishing", "Hunting", "Gun Holsters, Cases & Bags", "Gun Holsters"]], "price": 19.95}}
{"item_id": "B00A1W9P5S", "title": "Brass Stacker Front Sight Adapter for Mosin Nagant M9130", "description": "Front Sight Adapter Ring allows for the use Original Post & Globe front sight (that has been removed during barrel shortening) of a Mosin Nagant 91/30 without permanent modification to firearm. Requirements: You must measure your barrel length correctly in order to choose the proper model. Barrel length is measured from the end of the barrel to the closed bolt face. (Always practice proper handling techniques, safety precautions, and ensure an UNLOADED condition before attempting to measure barrel length.) Close and lock bolt on UNLOADED chamber. Insert a \" diameter wooden dowel or other appropriate reference device that will not damage barrel into rifle bore from muzzle end until contact with closed bolt face. Mark dowel at end of barrel, remove dowel and use tape measure or yard stick determine barrel length. Use marked dowel to approximate the Final Fit Position of the Front Sight Adapter Ring model you select. Ensure that you check for any interference the Front Sight Adapter Ring may have with your forearm stock. The Front Sight Adapter Ring is \" thick. The standard, unmodified Mosin Nagant 9130 barrel is tapered along its length and is approximately 28.75\" long. The forward face of the original front sight is at approximately 27.70\". Therefore the forward barrel exposure is approximately 1.05\" (forward barrel exposure is length of barrel that extends beyond the front sight). FSAR nominal I.D. sizes: -A).6094\", -B).6250\", -C).6406\", -D).6563\", -E).6719\". Due to original barrel manufacturing techniques, some degree of inconsistency in barrel tapers may exist. Therefore, the Final Fit Positions given for the Front Sight Adapter Ring are approximations only and may vary depending on individual barrel taper. Complete instructions are supplied. for more information on selecting the correct Model number and installation please look for the Example in the extra images or visit http://brassstacker.com/Mosin-Nagant-9130-Front-Sight-Adapter-MN-FSAR.html.", "text": "Brass Stacker Front Sight Adapter for Mosin Nagant M9130 Front Sight Adapter Ring allows for the use Original Post & Globe front sight (that has been removed during barrel shortening) of a Mosin Nagant 91/30 without permanent modification to firearm. Requirements: You must measure your barrel length correctly in order to choose the proper model. Barrel length is measured from the end of the barrel to the closed bolt face. (Always practice proper handling techniques, safety precautions, and ensure an UNLOADED condition before attempting to measure barrel length.) Close and lock bolt on UNLOADED chamber. Insert a \" diameter wooden dowel or other appropriate reference device that will not damage barrel into rifle bore from muzzle end until contact with closed bolt face. Mark dowel at end of barrel, remove dowel and use tape measure or yard stick determine barrel length. Use marked dowel to approximate the Final Fit Position of the Front Sight Adapter Ring model you select. Ensure that you check for any interference the Front Sight Adapter Ring may have with your forearm stock. The Front Sight Adapter Ring is \" thick. The standard, unmodified Mosin Nagant 9130 barrel is tapered along its length and is approximately 28.75\" long. The forward face of the original front sight is at approximately 27.70\". Therefore the forward barrel exposure is approximately 1.05\" (forward barrel exposure is length of barrel that extends beyond the front sight). FSAR nominal I.D. sizes: -A).6094\", -B).6250\", -C).6406\", -D).6563\", -E).6719\". Due to original barrel manufacturing techniques, some degree of inconsistency in barrel tapers may exist. Therefore, the Final Fit Positions given for the Front Sight Adapter Ring are approximations only and may vary depending on individual barrel taper. Complete instructions are supplied. for more information on selecting the correct Model number and installation please look for the Example in the extra images or visit http://brassstacker.com/Mosin-Nagant-9130-Front-Sight-Adapter-MN-FSAR.html.", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/31PQvJnpt%2BL._SX300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B00A1W9P5S.jpg", "metadata": {"categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Hunting & Fishing", "Hunting"]]}}
{"item_id": "B00A1WC2B2", "title": "Brass Stacker Cocking Knob Safety Pull Ring for Mosin Nagant", "description": "Inconvenient at best, the cocking knob safety of the Mosin Nagant can be difficult to engage and is therefore often not used. In an effort to promote firearm safety by preventing accidental discharge, we have developed our Cocking Knob Safety Pull Ring (Patent Pending) which allows for more convenient manipulation of the Mosin Nagant safety. ***There is wide variation in cocking knob diameter, thickness and crown radius in the Mosin Nagant population. In addition, there are many cases where the cocking knob neck is bent. We have made every reasonable effort to ensure that this product will fit the majority of Mosin Nagant cocking knobs. However, due to the large number of these firearms produced over many years around the world, it is impossible for us to allow for all manufacturing variation. As with all of our products, it may be returned undamaged for a full refund. This product does not fix, repair, replace, improve or in any way change the condition or function of your firearms' existing safety. It is designed to simply allow for easier manipulation the existing safety. NEVER depend solely on your firearms' safety, ALWAYS keep your firearm pointed in a safe direction. Operating Instructions: CAUTION! Engage / disengage safety ONLY with rifle pointed in a SAFE direction! With the Safety Pull Ring properly installed and fingers AWAY from trigger, engage the safety from a cocked condition by inserting finger securely in ring, gently pull cocking knob rearward and rotate counterclockwise approximately 45. To disengage the safety, insert finger securely in ring, gently pull cocking knob rearward and rotate clockwise back to a vertical position. CAUTION! Improper installation or use may result in damage to property, severe injury, or loss of life. If for any reason this product does not function properly with your firearm, discontinue use immediately.", "text": "Brass Stacker Cocking Knob Safety Pull Ring for Mosin Nagant Inconvenient at best, the cocking knob safety of the Mosin Nagant can be difficult to engage and is therefore often not used. In an effort to promote firearm safety by preventing accidental discharge, we have developed our Cocking Knob Safety Pull Ring (Patent Pending) which allows for more convenient manipulation of the Mosin Nagant safety. ***There is wide variation in cocking knob diameter, thickness and crown radius in the Mosin Nagant population. In addition, there are many cases where the cocking knob neck is bent. We have made every reasonable effort to ensure that this product will fit the majority of Mosin Nagant cocking knobs. However, due to the large number of these firearms produced over many years around the world, it is impossible for us to allow for all manufacturing variation. As with all of our products, it may be returned undamaged for a full refund. This product does not fix, repair, replace, improve or in any way change the condition or function of your firearms' existing safety. It is designed to simply allow for easier manipulation the existing safety. NEVER depend solely on your firearms' safety, ALWAYS keep your firearm pointed in a safe direction. Operating Instructions: CAUTION! Engage / disengage safety ONLY with rifle pointed in a SAFE direction! With the Safety Pull Ring properly installed and fingers AWAY from trigger, engage the safety from a cocked condition by inserting finger securely in ring, gently pull cocking knob rearward and rotate counterclockwise approximately 45. To disengage the safety, insert finger securely in ring, gently pull cocking knob rearward and rotate clockwise back to a vertical position. CAUTION! Improper installation or use may result in damage to property, severe injury, or loss of life. If for any reason this product does not function properly with your firearm, discontinue use immediately.", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/41CyiyXmfkL._SX300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B00A1WC2B2.jpg", "metadata": {"brand": "Brass Stacker", "categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Hunting & Fishing", "Hunting"]], "price": 47.95}}
{"item_id": "B00A1WEMRE", "title": "Trapezoid Grip Slide Lock for Glock Pistols", "description": "Don't be fooled by the imitators! This is the ORIGINAL Trapezoid Grip™ slide lock for Glock™ pistols. Unfortunately there are \"knock offs\", copies and counterfeit versions on the market. Ensure yours is genuine Brass Stacker™ Brand! The Brass Stacker Slide Lock is shaped to allow for maximum finger grip making field strip take down a breeze. The low profile design is approximately flush with the pistol frame reducing holster wear and the general discomfort found with extended slide locks. We manufacture theses from aircraft grade 4130 chrome-moly alloy steel and mill the barrel lug notch for superior \"in battery\" lock up. Made in America by Brass Stacker with a 100% Lifetime Warranty. Will not work with Glock 36 or 42 models. Free domestic shipping.", "text": "Trapezoid Grip Slide Lock for Glock Pistols Don't be fooled by the imitators! This is the ORIGINAL Trapezoid Grip™ slide lock for Glock™ pistols. Unfortunately there are \"knock offs\", copies and counterfeit versions on the market. Ensure yours is genuine Brass Stacker™ Brand! The Brass Stacker Slide Lock is shaped to allow for maximum finger grip making field strip take down a breeze. The low profile design is approximately flush with the pistol frame reducing holster wear and the general discomfort found with extended slide locks. We manufacture theses from aircraft grade 4130 chrome-moly alloy steel and mill the barrel lug notch for superior \"in battery\" lock up. Made in America by Brass Stacker with a 100% Lifetime Warranty. Will not work with Glock 36 or 42 models. Free domestic shipping.", "image_url": "http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/51rJW1jHfUL._SX300_.jpg", "image_path": "data/images/sports/B00A1WEMRE.jpg", "metadata": {"categories": [["Sports & Outdoors", "Hunting & Fishing", "Hunting", "Gun Holsters, Cases & Bags", "Gun Holsters"]], "price": 12.0}}
